    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
         2. THE CHALLENGE & THE BRIEF
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="ks-section">
        <div class="ks-container">
            <span class="ks-section-label">01 / The Challenge</span>
            <h2 class="ks-section-h2">From Dusty Archives to an Organic Playground</h2>
            
            <p class="ks-body-text">
                Traditional Indian games—from <em>Pachisi</em> and <em>Gilli Danda</em> to forgotten regional board games 
                like <em>Terhuchü</em> and <em>We-Dyuta</em>—are fading from public memory. Khol Khel’s core mission 
                is reviving these cultural traditions through craftsmanship and storytelling.
            </p>

            <div class="ks-callout-card">
                <p>
                    "The client had documented over 75 games across India with complex rules, historical lineages, and cultural contexts. 
                    A standard e-commerce grid or alphabetized list would strip away the very soul of play. 
                    The challenge was to design an intuitive mental model where users feel like they are exploring, not researching."
                </p>
                <small>— Design Objective</small>
            </div>

            <div class="ks-split-grid">
                <div>
                    <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--ks-moss-deep); margin-bottom: 12px;">The Core Problems</h3>
                    <ul style="list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;">
                        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark" style="color: var(--ks-clay); margin-top: 4px;"></i>
                            <span><strong>Information Overload:</strong> 75 games with varied density—some have simple 2-line rules, while others carry centuries of archaeological evidence.</span>
                        </li>
                        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark" style="color: var(--ks-clay); margin-top: 4px;"></i>
                            <span><strong>Contextual Disconnection:</strong> In traditional play, games are tied to places—courtyards, temple floors, school lanes, open fields. Flat lists erase this spatial emotion.</span>
                        </li>
                        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark" style="color: var(--ks-clay); margin-top: 4px;"></i>
                            <span><strong>Discoverability vs. Utility:</strong> Users who want to casually browse need delightful serendipity, while educators and game enthusiasts need immediate search and filtering.</span>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--ks-moss); margin-bottom: 12px;">The Strategic Solution</h3>
                    <ul style="list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;">
                        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check" style="color: var(--ks-moss); margin-top: 4px;"></i>
                            <span><strong>Spatial Navigation:</strong> Designed an illustrated interactive "Playground" map as the mental anchor. Users pan and zoom naturally across familiar childhood settings.</span>
                        </li>
                        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check" style="color: var(--ks-moss); margin-top: 4px;"></i>
                            <span><strong>Hierarchical Taxonomy:</strong> Grouped 75 games into 9 physical & intellectual zones (Buddhiyoga, Aim & Pocket, Family, Gully, Dodge & Tag, Strike & Field, Sports, Yoga, Buddhibala).</span>
                        </li>
                        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check" style="color: var(--ks-moss); margin-top: 4px;"></i>
                            <span><strong>Dual-Mode Access:</strong> Combined free-roam visual exploration with a lightning-fast filter drawer for users searching by player count, genre, or region.</span>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
         3. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="ks-section">
        <div class="ks-container">
